          "name": "disabled",
          "type": "Boolean",
          "description": "Disabled = The machine is complete disabled, down for some reason and unable to produce.\n\nThis flag generally will correspond to either Planned or Unplanned Downtime - but not 100% of the time will planned or unplanned events result in the machine being completely disabled and unable to produce.\n\nThis flag is used to calculate 'run time' for OEE in addition to the includeInOee flag on your Mode table.\n\nTypically, to consider the machine disabled, the event should last several minutes. Short stoppages, less than several minutes are generally not included in OEE calculations by most standard definitions.",
